<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erhard von Queis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1529</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erhard von Queis was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Pomesania in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> from 1523 until his death in 1529. A lawyer from Silesia, he adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> and introduced reforms in his diocese. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>'s state became the secular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a> in 1525, he surrendered his secular rule to Duke Albert in 1527.</p></div>
